# Repository-root .dockerignore
# -----------------------------
# Every connector image now builds with the REPOSITORY ROOT as its context
# (docker build -f <Connector>/Dockerfile .), because each references
# ../Connector.Chassis and a build cannot reach outside its context. Docker only
# ever reads the .dockerignore at the context root, so the per-connector files
# stopped being honoured the moment the context moved — including their exclusion
# of env/.env.local, which holds real credentials on a developer machine.
#
# This file restores those exclusions for the whole repository. Patterns are
# **/-prefixed so they apply inside every connector directory.

# Build output (rebuilt inside the image)
**/bin/
**/obj/

# Version control
.git
.gitignore

# Runtime artifacts / state (bind-mounted or created at runtime, never baked in)
**/logs/
**/data/
**/stress-out/

# IDE / user files
**/.vs/
**/.idea/
**/*.user

# Local environment / secrets — never copy real credentials into the image.
# The tracked .env.local.example templates are deliberately NOT matched.
**/env/.env.local
**/env/.env.local.user
**/.env.local
**/.env.local.user

# Container / CI descriptors (not needed inside the build context)
**/docker-compose.yml
**/docker-compose.*.yml
.github/
